[0.022027, "o", "======================================================================\r\nSCENARIO 1: Result 1 counterexample, reproduced (no barrier)\r\n======================================================================\r\n"]
[0.022172, "o", "\r\n-- Final state --\r\n  Node(N1, ledger=[\"b2\"], spent=[\"b1\"])\r\n  Node(N2, ledger=[\"b2\"], spent=[\"b1\"])\r\n  Node(N3, ledger=[], spent=[])\r\n\r\nNoDoubleSpendAcrossNodes violations: [(\"b1\", [\"N1\", \"N2\"])]\r\nCONFIRMED: same double-spend shape as the addendum's Result 1 trace.\r\n\r\n======================================================================\r\nSCENARIO 2: Same setup, but Conversion Day barrier intervenes\r\n======================================================================\r\n\r\n>> Conversion Day barrier fires (coordinator reconciles all nodes) <<\r\n\r\n-- State immediately after Conversion Day --\r\n  Node(N1, ledger=[\"b2\"], spent=[\"b1\"])\r\n  Node(N2, ledger=[\"b2\"], spent=[])\r\n  Node(N3, ledger=[], spent=[])\r\n\r\nN2 attempted to spend b1 and was correctly rejected: N2 does not hold b1, cannot spend\r\n\r\ncheck_post_barrier_safety(): true\r\nCONFIRMED: Conversion Day closes exactly the gap Result 1/2 describe.\r\n\r\n======================================================================\r\nSCENARIO 3: Barrier correctly detects a re"]
[0.022199, "o", "al pre-existing double-spend\r\n======================================================================\r\n"]
[0.022308, "o", "\r\nConversion Day correctly detected an unresolvable conflict: double-spend detected during reconciliation: [(\"b1\", [\"N1\", \"N2\"])]\r\n(This is what has to be escalated out-of-band -- the barrier\r\n prevents FUTURE double-spends, it cannot undo one that\r\n already completed before the barrier ran.)\r\n\r\n======================================================================\r\nAll scenarios completed.\r\n======================================================================\r\n"]
